{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why","id":1248602,"title":"Favorite bloodlines and why","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-21T19:51:54-07:00","id":1248602,"title":"Favorite bloodlines and why","content":"For me, it would have to be the carnival, players, and macellarius<br /> <br /> For the first, it's because at first I thought it was ridiculous they were a daeva clan (I was ignorant of the fact not everything should adhere to a set standard at the time) but when I read about them, it all made sense! They performed to small, personal crowds and, unlike the nosferatu, were meant to be the center of the show, winning the crowd through their freakish nature, not scare them into wanting to run. Lastly, i really like the road trip feel you can give them, and the little society they have within it<br /> <br /> For the players, i simply loved how there were a bloodline of losers. That may sound weird, but the fact there is a bloodline tied to the HIGHLY romanticized view young people have of vampires is great to deconstructed in such a way as to make fun of it (looking at you, twilight). But also, i like how you can still play them tragically (or even, perhaps more fittingly, with angst) having to learn that being a vampire sucks, that they miss their old lives as regular humans merely fantasizing about fame and fortune, not groveling for taste of human blood. Lastly, I like that they are essentially the underdogs, and had a blast playing with one who managed to not only reached a high place in the invictus (with our help) but did so by threatening to unleash the &quot;secret weapon&quot; of the players (my friend who played as him managed learn about their reputation)<br /> <br /> Lastly the gentlemen and women, the macellarius. Great lore, and a new kind of horror. Sure we've seen the gentlemanly hedonist (or just inbred hillbilly family) but never have we (or just me, perhaps) seen vampires that are simply obese, cannibalistic to much more than blood, yet so courteous as to be frightening, a gruesome showing of the dark, corrupt, twisted reflection of &quot;life&quot; vampires have to humans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T07:24:57-07:00","id":1248703,"title":"","content":"I agree with you about the Macellarius, but that's about it really.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't like the traditional way Bloodlines are done. It seems like more of a holdover from how Masq did things, and I think that contributed to the bloat in Masq.<br /> <br /> As far as types of Vampires, I prefer to keep the game focused on the 5 archetypal clans. When it comes to some of the cool powers available to Bloodlines, I think more often they work better as new Covenants with their power as Covenant perks, or integrate them into existing Covenants and powers, like the Gethsemani and LeS integrated into Theban, or the Architects of the Monolith could be integrated into the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> When I do like to use bloodlines, I prefer to use local bloodlines that are more like family broods of sires and childer, only using the 10 standard disciplnes to mix things up and add flavor.<br /> <br /> *edit* I also really like the Bohagande. The lore and the luck powers are very cool, but yeah, even them, cooler as a Covenant for me, maybe one that passes on the luck curse to other vamps they encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","user":"nicodemus","date":". 08-22-2018, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T08:21:01-07:00","id":1248713,"title":"","content":"Well, I like to play unconventional types of characters when I see an opportunity to do so. So my favorite bloodlines include a list of some of the more difficult or rare bloodlines you're likely to come across.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the <b>Cockscomb Society</b>, a bloodline of Nosferatu who don't allow their deformity to stop them from living the high life. I think they make a compelling argument for your appearance and behavior don't matter, as long as you're rich as hell!<br /> <br /> <br /> I also like the <b>Niktuku</b>, due to the concept of the hunter becoming the hunted. They can be very effective as both a plot hook, as well as an important NPC. Make a Niktuku your Sheriff and watch as the Prince rules the city with an iron fist.<br /> <br /> <br /> The <b>Carnon</b> of the Gangrel are also cool with their 'Horned God' motif. I've always been a little fascinated with the figure, even if I'm not as knowledgeable about them as I'd like to be. Plus there's some really good potential for a Circle of the Crone focused story hook, or even chronicle when it comes to these guys.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, I think I also enjoy the <b>Gorgons</b> and their snake fetish powers. Plus the fact that they are Ventrue makes them immediately stand out to me, as I typically don't associate the clan of royalty with a hideous monster like Medusa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T10:40:21-07:00","id":1248741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1248713#post1248713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I like to play unconventional types of characters when I see an opportunity to do so. So my favorite bloodlines include a list of some of the more difficult or rare bloodlines you're likely to come across.<br /> <br /> <br /> The <b>Carnon</b> of the Gangrel are also cool with their 'Horned God' motif. I've always been a little fascinated with the figure, even if I'm not as knowledgeable about them as I'd like to be. Plus there's some really good potential for a Circle of the Crone focused story hook, or even chronicle when it comes to these</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope these guys get more lore, i was surprised they weren't in bloodlines the legendary.<br /> <br /> As for the cockscomb society, i love the full out defiance they have to the clan curse, they may be nightmare incarnate, but they won't let that keep them from fanciful living. However, i think the bloodline curse is a bit much, but they ARE negating their clan curse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T10:52:59-07:00","id":1248748,"title":"","content":"<b>Icarians</b>, they make greats Self assured Villains<br /> <br /> (I have a hard time rooting for the Chapel and the spear im afraid)<br /> <br /> <br /> The <b>Galloi </b>As a reminder that beauty is only skin deep<br /> <br /> The <b>Yagnata </b>the vibe just appealed to me.<br /> <br /> I also like the <b>Gorgons</b> As Royalty basicly within the circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T12:17:23-07:00","id":1248759,"title":"","content":"I'm overly fond of Mekhet and Nosferatu bloodlines.<br /> <br /> For Mekhet (aka the best clan don't @ me), the <b>Morbus </b>and the <b>Alucinor </b>both touch on interesting aspects of the Shadow archetype. Also pretty much any of the bloodlines from <b>Shadows in the Dark</b>. And of course, fan favourite the <b>Khaibit</b>.<br /> <br /> Despite not being a clan I've ever played, Nosferatu have a great lineup. The <b>Morotrophians</b>, the <b>Baddacelli</b>, the <b>Galloi</b>, the <b>Noctuku</b>...so many grave blooms to choose from, even from a small garden. The Nosferatu were a bit neglected for bloodlines, but they always had some of the coolest.<br /> <br /> For Ventrue, <b>R\u00f6tgrafen </b>are always fun. I like the ones where the line between the Lords and the Gangrel blur.<br /> <br /> For Daeva, the <b>Tianpan</b> <b>Xiao </b>and the <b>Zelani</b>. I like the former for being a creepy twist on the Daeva obsession with humanity, and the latter for being a real &quot;What the fuck?&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> For Gangrel, the <b>Annunaku </b>are a cool against-stereotype type of bloodline, while still definitely fulfilling the stereotype. I'm also a fan of area effect powers. Oh, and the <b>Oberlochs</b> -- see above on blurring lines between Ventrue and Gangrel.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T13:05:06-07:00","id":1248767,"title":"","content":"The relationship between gangrel and ventrue has always been interesting to me, and I do like the bloodlines that make use of their relations<br /> <br /> Also, the Bron's curse. While it would probably need plenty of storyteller changes, possible divine fire interacting with the stasis of the undead?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar241_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"241\" data-vbnamecard=\"241\">nicodemus</a> I can see why you see it that way. In terms of viewing them in a more negative and positive light, my groups storyteller personally sees them as either being cartoonish, splintering the clans into too many sub groups, or just as simply stupid. That last one comes from the players, but that opinion has changed somewhat when we started an episodic chronicle composed of just players, and was semi serious satire for mood, and an ironic self awareness for tone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 08-22-2018, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T13:32:44-07:00","id":1250312,"title":"","content":"Just wondering, will there be another book akin to the bloodlines the legendary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T15:47:28-07:00","id":1250339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1250312#post1250312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering, will there be another book akin to the bloodlines the legendary?</div> </div> </div> </div>The current &quot;bloodlines book&quot; in the pipeline is <b>Spilled Blood</b>, the next Night Horrors for Vampire, but it also includes lost clans and other [REDACTED]. I don't know if any exclusively bloodlines-focused books are in the cards for the future, but I know an update of the Bron is forthcoming in Dark Eras 2 <s>The Revenge</s><br /> <br /> On a related note, I'm planning on posting a few 1e Bloodlines updates in the near future, some of them from <b>Legendary</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T15:51:41-07:00","id":1250340,"title":"","content":"Oh ok thanks! Also damn, Requiem will have 3 night horrors books<br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>, the galloi discipline can be used on themselves right, or can it only be used on another vampire/mortal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 08-31-2018, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T18:59:35-07:00","id":1250370,"title":"","content":"Spilled Blood is not a Night Horrors book.<br /> <br /> If I've understood correctly the current philosophy at OPP is that they won't release pure Y-splat books. They will instead be introduced in other supplements, like Morbus in Dark Eras Companion and some bloodlines in Spilled Blood that we'll hopefully see in about a year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-31T19:17:35-07:00","id":1250373,"title":"","content":"Oh ok, i misunderstood the spilled blood book.<br /> <br /> Aren't Y-splats things such as covenants? I've heard bloodlines and lodges be called Z-splats, but that could just be to differentiate themselves by fans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T00:55:48-07:00","id":1250416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1250370#post1250370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spilled Blood is not a Night Horrors book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, it is indeed a Night Horrors book, having worked on it for the past few months. That\u2019s what\u2019s on my outline, at least. This wasn\u2019t a secret or anything; it was referred to as such in the most recent Reddit AMA (and a few other places, I believe). I don\u2019t think it\u2019s been explicitly called that on the blog, though, so it could be the title was changed somewhere along the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-01-2018, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T02:42:30-07:00","id":1250423,"title":"","content":"Really? That half of the title of the book is just missing from the Current Projects page and the MMNs, unlike Shunned, Tormented and Nameless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T11:00:08-07:00","id":1250486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1250423#post1250423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? That half of the title of the book is just missing from the Current Projects page and the MMNs, unlike Shunned, Tormented and Nameless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like I said, it may be something changed along the line. It\u2019ll certainly read like a Night Horrors book, regardless of branding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-01T11:40:23-07:00","id":1250495,"title":"","content":"Cool, the bloodlines are in my opinion the most well done Z-splats (that is what they are called right)?<br /> <br /> Also, a ventrue player in my group is thinking about becoming a macellarius, are there any tips for playing as one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T09:54:17-07:00","id":1250797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nicodemus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1248703#post1248703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to some of the cool powers available to Bloodlines, I think more often they work better as new Covenants with their power as Covenant perks, or integrate them into existing Covenants and powers, like the Gethsemani and LeS integrated into Theban, or the Architects of the Monolith could be integrated into the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> When I do like to use bloodlines, I prefer to use local bloodlines that are more like family broods of sires and childer, only using the 10 standard disciplnes to mix things up and add flavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot to be said for all that. I think the Architects of the Monolith work well as a separate covenant rooted in a fusion of Ordo and Invictus ideas - vampires becoming the very currents of power that flow through cities. The interesting thing about the Tismanu is their cultural role within the Ordo Dracul, so they could be a faction as much as a bloodline. The Alucinor archetype could be a fascinating addition to <i>any</i> clan, which makes them a feasible covenant. The Toreador could be considered &quot;socially local&quot; even if they're not geographically so.<br /> <br /> I like the Annunaki, Malocusians, and Morotrophians - along with Tenure, Domus, and Institutionalise (three very atmospheric Disciplines) - and all three together seem like a similar kind of change expressing itself in different ways for each clan. It would be interesting to see what the Daeva and Mekhet analogues would be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T13:19:13-07:00","id":1250831,"title":"","content":"I think there are many cool bloodlines that has me much more interested than most Legacies or Lodges, but I have a problem with bloodlines as a concept. New quirks of the blood, blood borne curses, dynasties with little to no mechanics, and Covenant sub-factions all share this single slot on the character sheet. Those are all cool things I want to see in VTR, but by making them all fit into the same mould they all get the same mechanical status and are directly compared despite filling wildly different roles in the game.<br /> Since only a single bloodline has been published in a book in 2e I have a faint hope that Spilled Blood will revise the system for bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T13:32:39-07:00","id":1250834,"title":"","content":"I've heard that exact problem from my groups storyteller, whenever we get accepted into a bloodline, the vampire in game will set a date for the embrace ceremony kinda deal. In reality this is just so he can home brew how the bloodlines mechanics would be 2nd edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T14:33:46-07:00","id":1250851,"title":"","content":"Toreador, Taifa and Galloi<br /> <br /> Daeva are passionate, for sure, but that passion is not always focused on arts and art patronage like the Toreador of Masquerade, having a bloodline which focused on that is a nice touch regardless if it was a nod to the previous game or not. Also plenty of concept ideas.<br /> <br /> As an ethnic Arab I'm very grateful for the Taifa, really, for the first time I'm glad to see Muslims and Arabs depicted as art and culture patrons rather than bloodthirsty terrorists (cough cough Assamite).<br /> <br /> I didn't like the Galloi when I first read about them in Bloodlines: The Legendary, though I completely changed my opinion when, in one game, there was a family of Galloi who were a powerful line of Harpies in Venice; the snark, the snobbery, the way one of them completely eradicated my character for making a simple social faux pas in Elysium; absolutely amazing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T10:19:17-07:00","id":1251091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1250831#post1250831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New quirks of the blood,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Morbus - in both Discipline and weakness - draw from a definite vampire archetype, which can refine the Mekhet's (diseases are invisible) (it could refine the Nosferatu too, as diseases are fearsome, but doesn't really make sense for the other three).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> blood borne curses, </div> </div> </div>The Nelapsi are like a clan or clanlet beginning to break down - a terrible weakness that drives them out of almost any vampiric society. It makes sense for it to be confined to one clan, but it could be any of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> dynasties with little to no mechanics, and </div> </div> </div>The Toreador are built around a shared cultural impulse that seems like something that would pass from sire to childe - in the sense that it would be a strong influence on the kind of person the sire Embraces - but is more or less orthogonal to most of the things covenants offer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Covenant sub-factions all share this single slot on the character sheet. </div> </div> </div>Cf the Tismanu in my post. Spiritual counselors for a covenant that regards God as an obstacle is a great concept, and one of the ways the Ordo's history is appropriately messy. But I can't remember what clan they are, or anything about their Discipline - and it makes little sense for them to be confined to one clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T12:51:19-07:00","id":1251148,"title":"","content":"I liked the concept of Alucinor as vampiric sandmen, and the possibility of preying and toying with the human (and inhuman) psyche. Note this bloodline was conceived years before Mage and Changeling were a thing. Sadly, its backstory was lackluster and the discipline needed a bit of retooling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 09-03-2018, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T13:19:54-07:00","id":1251153,"title":"","content":"Very understandable, especially now with beast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T12:58:08-07:00","id":1253675,"title":"","content":"Melissidae and Morbus. Morbus are just cool, and are a great example of Z-axis change to a character that completely alters the way they play, while still staying in the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> The Melissidae are just excellent. It's the Ventrue need for control tuned to an excessive degree. As a PC, even if your character wants to run from their fate, they are forced, night by night, down the path of their predecessor. As an NPC, great for throwing your players for a loop, and an excellent Big Bad, with some nice body and psychological horror thrown in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24624-vtheunreliable","user":"VTheUnreliable","date":".  Edited for clarity 09-12-2018, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24624-vtheunreliable","name":"VTheUnreliable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T04:35:45-07:00","id":1253841,"title":"","content":"I like Macellari, Galloi, Taifa, Morbus, Lygos, Deucalion y Nelapsi. Anything I can use as a terrifying NPC.<br /> <br /> Once I had a setting prepared for a VTM/VTR mixed game that included over 30 different &quot;bloodlines&quot; (the word &quot;bloodline&quot; would substitute &quot;clan&quot; in-game). Of course, the vampire couldn't convert from bloodline to bloodline, only by embrace or in weird cases of diablerie... Anyway, the point is, I used many of the Requiem Bloodlines to create other clans, but in some instances I would mix and match bloodlines together that I consider thematically redundant to create historical narratives for some of them. For instance,<br /> -- Lygos+Badacelli were one, Lygos were a bloodline of blind light averting pale-translucent underdwellers with tales and rumors of their existence stretching back to the Grand Covenant of Egypt and ties to Anubian cults. <br /> -- Orlok- was the name for VTM Nosferatu,<br /> -- Kerberos and Taifa were the same line of Social Predators but spit into two groups when they assimilated themselves to greek and persian culture respectably. <br /> -- Mabry are the lost descendants of a long lost Gangrel linage of hunnic warlords who traded Protean for Vigor. After Rome's fall these vamps joined the legio mortuum and the gallow posts, spreading throughout Europe settling isolated spider traps. and eventually almost died out. One lone survivor with low humanity, got to the US and embraced the remaining Mabry family abandoning them right after.<br /> -- The Anvari and Ishtarri share common ancestry<br /> -- The Impundulu were actually an odd type of Striges that the african witches were able to blind into servitude, looking like lightning birds instead of owls... that's all I remember off top of my head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12201-brainstr\u00f6m","name":"Brainstr\u00f6m","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T13:27:12-07:00","id":1253990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brainstr\u00f6m</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1248602-favorite-bloodlines-and-why?p=1253841#post1253841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Macellari, Galloi, Taifa, Morbus, Lygos, Deucalion y Nelapsi. Anything I can use as a terrifying NPC.<br /> <br /> Once I had a setting prepared for a VTM/VTR mixed game that included over 30 different &quot;bloodlines&quot; (the word &quot;bloodline&quot; would substitute &quot;clan&quot; in-game). Of course, the vampire couldn't convert from bloodline to bloodline, only by embrace or in weird cases of diablerie... Anyway, the point is, I used many of the Requiem Bloodlines to create other clans, but in some instances I would mix and match bloodlines together that I consider thematically redundant to create historical narratives for some of them. For instance,<br /> -- Lygos+Badacelli were one, Lygos were a bloodline of blind light averting pale-translucent underdwellers with tales and rumors of their existence stretching back to the Grand Covenant of Egypt and ties to Anubian cults.<br /> -- Orlok- was the name for VTM Nosferatu,<br /> -- Kerberos and Taifa were the same line of Social Predators but spit into two groups when they assimilated themselves to greek and persian culture respectably.<br /> -- Mabry are the lost descendants of a long lost Gangrel linage of hunnic warlords who traded Protean for Vigor. After Rome's fall these vamps joined the legio mortuum and the gallow posts, spreading throughout Europe settling isolated spider traps. and eventually almost died out. One lone survivor with low humanity, got to the US and embraced the remaining Mabry family abandoning them right after.<br /> -- The Anvari and Ishtarri share common ancestry<br /> -- The Impundulu were actually an odd type of Striges that the african witches were able to blind into servitude, looking like lightning birds instead of owls... that's all I remember off top of my head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you want creepy NPCs for your players, you can\u00b4t go wrong with Badacelli. Specially in underground locations like sewers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-13T14:26:19-07:00","id":1254000,"title":"","content":"While I dislike the concept of mechanical bloodlines, especially with peculiar disciplines, I do like some bloodlines individually:<ul><li>Norvegi: a vestige of a near exinct clan that's assimilated into another. I think that I'd interested in seeing a Jiang Shi bloodline for a similar reason.</li> <li>Ordo Dracul ones in general: The old ones show a bit of regional witchcraft, spirituality and so forth that apparently forms part of Ordo Dracul's background. The new ones tend to be focussed around new avenues of reasearch. But I prefer them as Y-subsplats. However, I do think that Ordo Dracul has an excuse to make new bloodlines because changing their state of vampirism is what they do.</li> <li>Moroi: Sort of the two reasons above combined.</li> <li>Melissidae: One of most instantly scary features of V:tR in my opinion.</li> <li>Bron: Basically because they might have been the Welsh clan (I'm bit biased towards other Welsh things sometimes, very much including Beddnerys) at some point before anyone around there had heard of Ventrue. Or maybe it's a load of reconstructed b******s based on the Matter of Britain that makes them feel special, but either way, I'm interested.</li> <li>Players and Carnon: I don't how to explain it, I just like them.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[